 "display": {
  "title": "Episode 204: Little Avraham",
  "title_basis": "master_catalog",
  "summary_short": "The My Mezuzah contest winners are announced, a young guest leads the Shema, and Uncle Yossi tells how little Avraham searched the sun, moon and stars until he found Hashem.",
  "summary_long": "Uncle Yossi announces the results of the My Mezuzah contest. The super grand winner is a long, richly decorated mezuzah from a family of his own nephews and nieces: inside the letters Shin, Dalet and Yud of Hashem's name they wrote the names of Uncle Yossi's brothers and sisters, whose father had chosen names that together spell Hashem's name, along with a drawing of the Kosel and a second mezuzah lettered like a sofer's. He then reads the long list of grand winners, who are asked to send photos for the Tzivos Hashem newsletter. After the Hakochainik march to 'Yibaneh Beis HaMikdash', a young boy, the son of an artist, leads the Shema, and his mother thanks the program. Story time tells of three-year-old Avraham walking by the sea, wondering who made the world. He thinks the sun might be G-d until it sets, then the moon, then the stars, and finally realizes there is one Creator who cannot be seen but is everywhere. He grows up to be Avraham Avinu, the first Jew. The show closes with a reminder about the Wonderful World of Shabbos exhibit.",
  "lesson": "There is only one Creator, who made the sun, moon and stars; like Avraham, keep searching for Hashem and proudly proclaim Shema Yisroel.",
